      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "The page says: “Physically normalized raw and smoothed estimates recover the unaliased value under the precise zero-noncentral-alias condition; spectra supported inside the Nyquist cube provide a sufficient case.” The in-scope corollary requires a bounded periodized-density representative continuous at the target and relies on the smoothing theorem, which requires b_n→0 and n b_n→∞; its support-based sufficient case also requires f to be continuous and supported in a compact subset of the open Nyquist cube. Support/no-alias alone does not suffice: for d=1, δ=1, and 0<a<π, take the even density f(ω)=1 for 0<|ω|<a and 0 otherwise. Its support is [−a,a] inside the Nyquist interval and every noncentral alias at ω₀=0 vanishes, but f(0)=0 while the Fejér expected raw periodogram at 0 tends to 1. The page therefore omits hypotheses essential even for expectation recovery; the corollary does not establish convergence of the estimates themselves.",
